      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's true that St. John's Wort is considered a natural supplement, its potent effects on the body, particularly on liver enzymes, can interact with other medications. Combining St. John's Wort with the pill may cause the contraceptive to become less effective, leading to unintended pregnancy. Additionally, the increased metabolism of the pill's hormones can also lead to uneven blood sugar levels, headaches, and other side effects. \n\nYour initial desire to avoid a doctor's appointment is understandable, but prioritizing your health and safety should take precedence.",
